  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.7900$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7900$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7881$ and $0.7910.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7881 & <0.7900<0.7910\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\u03a6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(0.80) & <\u03a6(z)<\u03a6(0.81).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz\u2248\\frac{0.80+0.81}{2}=0.805.\n$$",
